id: pm-memory-sdk-rule-1117
title: Accept additive SDK secret rules without weakening memory privacy
description: "The 2026.11.14 toolchain bump crosses the SDK 2026.11.13 credential_key_assignment addition, breaking the exhaustive consumer Record type."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-memory#79"
created_at: "2026-11-17T18:26:55.328Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T19:00:25.447Z"
author: codex-sol
repro_steps: npm run typecheck with the pm-toolchain update
expected_result: New SDK rules preserve type compatibility and refuse credential literals.
actual_result: TS2741 reports the missing credential_key_assignment policy.
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-17T18:30:56.656Z",codex-sol,"Job 133996528357 fails TS2741: SDK SecretGuardFinding.rule gained credential_key_assignment. The exhaustive Record made an additive SDK rule a consumer compile break. Use Partial with an explicit fail-closed default; real SDK positives remain refused and references remain allowed. An API-shape concern is recorded for the upstream draft."
  "2026-11-17T18:37:56.774Z",codex-sol,"Release notes refine the boundary: credential_key_assignment was introduced in SDK 2026.11.13 (GH-1704). The dependency branch jumps from 2026.11.11 to 2026.11.14, so both 2026.11.13 and 2026.11.14 reject the old exhaustive map. The upstream draft records an additive API-shape concern, not a claim that the new credential detection is incorrect."
  "2026-11-17T18:44:06.551Z",codex-sol,The original exhaustive map typechecks on the exact prior pin 2026.11.11 and fails on both 2026.11.13 and 2026.11.14. The new XML credential-key test isolates the SDK finding rather than the local assignment fallback; its pm-linked run passes. Typecheck and lint pass on the repaired policy.
  "2026-11-17T18:52:58.019Z",codex-sol,"The wider gate exposed an existing recall bug: Promise.all readUtility calls enter the same writer lease fence concurrently and can exhaust the SDK cleanup-gate wait with lock_lost. A fresh public SDK probe with twelve simultaneous fences reproduces 9 successes and 3 refusals on BOTH 2026.11.11 and 2026.11.14, so this is package misuse rather than a new SDK regression. Serialize the ledger reads before any counter writes; preserve every ownership fence and the original all-read-before-write boundary."
  "2026-11-17T18:58:03.071Z",codex-sol,"The real budget-property reproduction now passes after serializing ledger reads: 1 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped. Typecheck and lint pass on both source changes. The additive XML credential regression also passes through pm. The core-reference full-depth run and final recall-reference selection remain in progress; no full-suite pass is claimed."
  "2026-11-17T19:00:13.788Z",codex-sol,"Implementation/dependency commit: a6d62db. The original exhaustive SDK policy also compiles on 2026.11.12, establishing the immediate last-good type shape before 2026.11.13. The repaired real recall budget property passes directly; its final reference-file selection also reports that property passing. Replaced the expensive full-depth exploratory reference run with the same quick deterministic seed prefix used by CI, using the existing harness timeout scale; complete reference results remain pending."
files[6]{path,scope}:
  CHANGELOG.md,project
  package-lock.json,project
  package.json,project
  src/core.ts,project
